 "result": "Saved `scenario.json` for AR-CAL-22.\n\n**Request:** \"Change the time zone to America/New_York on the Ops Rotation calendar I own whose description mentions weekend on-call coverage.\" (target: `ops-noram@northwind.example`, PATCH `timeZone`)\n\n**Decoys** (all testing `A:Calendar.description`, the brief's required fact):\n- **Ops Rotation – EMEA** (F1, sibling attribute): its *location* field says \"Weekend on-call coverage rota posted here every Friday,\" but its description talks about staffing schedules — offers `Calendar.location` as the designated substitute.\n- **Ops Rotation – APAC** (F2, indirection): its own description is about daytime shift scheduling, but a reminder *event* on that calendar has a description mentioning weekend on-call coverage.\n- **Ops Rotation – LATAM** (F0, plain): same name pattern and ownership, but its description is about data-center maintenance windows — unrelated content.\n\nBackground/anchors: a \"Marketing Calendar\" (wrong name, owner, and description — fails 3 conditions) and an \"Ops Standup\" calendar (right owner, wrong name and description — fails 2 conditions) so they never compete as near-misses.",
